    {
      "@id": "concept:fair-work-act-2009-sch-1-sec-4",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "4 Fair work instruments etc. made before commencement",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/fair-work-act-2009#sch-1-sec-4"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "fair-work-act-2009.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "fair-work-act-2009.pdf, p.16",
      "values:originalText": "(1) This clause applies in relation to:\n\nApplication, saving and transitional provisions relating to amendments of this Act\nSchedule 1\nAmendments made by the Fair Work Amendment (Textile, Clothing and Footwear\nIndustry) Act 2012  Part 1\n\nClause 5\nFair Work Act 2009\nCompilation date: 02/04/2026\n(a) a fair work instrument made before commencement; or\n(b) a transitional instrument as continued in existence by\nSchedule 3 to the Transitional Act.\n(2) A reference in the instrument to an employee or an employer does\nnot include a deemed employee or a deemed employer, unless the\ninstrument is, after commencement, varied to make it clear that the\nreference is intended to include a deemed employee or deemed\nemployer.\n(3) This clause is not to be taken to confer a power to vary the\ninstrument.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) This clause applies in relation to:\n\nApplication, saving and transitional provisions relating to amendments of this Act\nSchedule 1\nAmendments made by the Fair Work Amendment (Textile, Clothing and Footwear\nIndustry) Act 2012  Part 1\n\nClause 5\nFair Work Act 2009\nCompilation date: 02/04/2026\n(a) a fair work instrument made before commencement; or\n(b) a transitional instrument as continued in existence by\nSchedule 3 to the Transitional Act.\n(2) A reference in the instrument to an employee or an employer does\nnot include a deemed employee or a deemed employer, unless the\ninstrument is, after commencement, varied to make it clear that the\nreference is intended to include a deemed employee or deemed\nemployer.\n(3) This clause is not to be taken to confer a power to vary the\ninstrument.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:fair-work-act-2009-sch-1-sec-4-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:fair-work-act-2009-sch-1-sec-4-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:fair-work-act-2009-sch-1-sec-4-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "f793a4c7eec00a62dd516ca070eb4bcec7fb7ceb16f1da754bafbb1079a4ffdd"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/fair-work-act-2009#sch-1-sec-4",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "4 Fair work instruments etc. made before commencement",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 16,
      "values:originalText": "(1) This clause applies in relation to:\n\nApplication, saving and transitional provisions relating to amendments of this Act\nSchedule 1\nAmendments made by the Fair Work Amendment (Textile, Clothing and Footwear\nIndustry) Act 2012  Part 1\n\nClause 5\nFair Work Act 2009\nCompilation date: 02/04/2026\n(a) a fair work instrument made before commencement; or\n(b) a transitional instrument as continued in existence by\nSchedule 3 to the Transitional Act.\n(2) A reference in the instrument to an employee or an employer does\nnot include a deemed employee or a deemed employer, unless the\ninstrument is, after commencement, varied to make it clear that the\nreference is intended to include a deemed employee or deemed\nemployer.\n(3) This clause is not to be taken to confer a power to vary the\ninstrument."
    },
