    {
      "@id": "concept:fair-work-act-2009-sch-1-sec-4-ss-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "4(2) Fair work instruments etc. made before commencement",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/fair-work-act-2009#sch-1-sec-4-ss-2"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "fair-work-act-2009.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "fair-work-act-2009.pdf, p.16",
      "values:originalText": "(2) A reference in the instrument to an employee or an employer does\nnot include a deemed employee or a deemed employer, unless the\ninstrument is, after commencement, varied to make it clear that the\nreference is intended to include a deemed employee or deemed\nemployer.",
      "skos:definition": "(2) A reference in the instrument to an employee or an employer does\nnot include a deemed employee or a deemed employer, unless the\ninstrument is, after commencement, varied to make it clear that the\nreference is intended to include a deemed employee or deemed\nemployer.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:fair-work-act-2009-sch-1-sec-4"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:fair-work-act-2009-sch-1-sec-4-ss-2-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:fair-work-act-2009-sch-1-sec-4-ss-2-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "688e4533ae95a11d0d2401545d5bb4860fe6802c7ba4a33faf89a0f3ab822c9f",
      "skos:note": "Deemed employee or employer references must be clarified after commencement."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/fair-work-act-2009#sch-1-sec-4-ss-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "4(2) Fair work instruments etc. made before commencement",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 16,
      "values:originalText": "(2) A reference in the instrument to an employee or an employer does\nnot include a deemed employee or a deemed employer, unless the\ninstrument is, after commencement, varied to make it clear that the\nreference is intended to include a deemed employee or deemed\nemployer."
    },
