    {
      "@id": "concept:fair-work-act-2009-sch-1-sec-25",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "25 Definitions",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/fair-work-act-2009#sch-1-sec-25"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "fair-work-act-2009.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "fair-work-act-2009.pdf, p.26",
      "values:originalText": "In this Part:\n4 yearly review of modern awards has the meaning given by this\nAct, as in force immediately before the commencement of\nSchedule 1 to the amending Act.\namended Act means this Act as amended by the amending Act.\namending Act means the Fair Work Amendment (Repeal of 4\nYearly Reviews and Other Measures) Act 2018.\nSchedule 1 commencement day means the day on which\nSchedule 1 to the amending Act commences.\nSchedule 2 commencement day means the day on which\nSchedule 2 to the amending Act commences.\n\nApplication, saving and transitional provisions relating to amendments of this Act\nSchedule 1\nAmendments made by the Fair Work Amendment (Repeal of 4 Yearly Reviews and\nOther Measures) Act 2018  Part 5\nAmendments made by Schedule 1 to the amending Act  Division 2\nClause 26\nFair Work Act 2009\nCompilation date: 02/04/2026",
      "skos:definition": "In this Part:\n4 yearly review of modern awards has the meaning given by this\nAct, as in force immediately before the commencement of\nSchedule 1 to the amending Act.\namended Act means this Act as amended by the amending Act.\namending Act means the Fair Work Amendment (Repeal of 4\nYearly Reviews and Other Measures) Act 2018.\nSchedule 1 commencement day means the day on which\nSchedule 1 to the amending Act commences.\nSchedule 2 commencement day means the day on which\nSchedule 2 to the amending Act commences.\n\nApplication, saving and transitional provisions relating to amendments of this Act\nSchedule 1\nAmendments made by the Fair Work Amendment (Repeal of 4 Yearly Reviews and\nOther Measures) Act 2018  Part 5\nAmendments made by Schedule 1 to the amending Act  Division 2\nClause 26\nFair Work Act 2009\nCompilation date: 02/04/2026",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:fair-work-act-2009-sch-1-sec-25-norm"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "6ce1473a7afab7e50aed53537f3cdd1a2ef38e9f3eaa5bf2fb6f69f30f8a18a1",
      "skos:note": "Definitions for Schedule 1"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/fair-work-act-2009#sch-1-sec-25",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "25 Definitions",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 26,
      "values:originalText": "In this Part:\n4 yearly review of modern awards has the meaning given by this\nAct, as in force immediately before the commencement of\nSchedule 1 to the amending Act.\namended Act means this Act as amended by the amending Act.\namending Act means the Fair Work Amendment (Repeal of 4\nYearly Reviews and Other Measures) Act 2018.\nSchedule 1 commencement day means the day on which\nSchedule 1 to the amending Act commences.\nSchedule 2 commencement day means the day on which\nSchedule 2 to the amending Act commences.\n\nApplication, saving and transitional provisions relating to amendments of this Act\nSchedule 1\nAmendments made by the Fair Work Amendment (Repeal of 4 Yearly Reviews and\nOther Measures) Act 2018  Part 5\nAmendments made by Schedule 1 to the amending Act  Division 2\nClause 26\nFair Work Act 2009\nCompilation date: 02/04/2026"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:fair-work-act-2009-sch-1-sec-25-norm",
      "@type": "values:Undertaking",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:fair-work-act-2009-sch-1-sec-25"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:fair-work-act-2009-sch-1-sec-26",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "26 Incomplete review of modern award",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/fair-work-act-2009#sch-1-sec-26"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "fair-work-act-2009.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "fair-work-act-2009.pdf, p.27",
      "values:originalText": "Scope\n(1) This clause applies in relation to a review of a modern award\nconducted as part of a 4 yearly review of modern awards if:\n(a) the review of the modern award commenced before the\nSchedule 1 commencement day; and\n(b) immediately before that day, the review of the modern award\nhad not been completed.\nSaving\n(2) Despite the repeal of:\n(a) Division 4 of Part 2-3 (which deals with 4 yearly reviews of\nmodern awards); and\n(b) paragraph 582(4)(a) (which deals with directions by the\nPresident); and\n(c) subsections 616(2) and (3) (which deal with the FWC’s\nfunctions etc. that must be performed by a Full Bench);\nby the amending Act, those provisions continue to apply, in\nrelation to the review of the modern award, as if those repeals had\nnot happened.\n(3) Despite the repeal of paragraph 582(4)(a) (which deals with\ndirections by the President) by the amending Act, a direction given\nby the President to an FWC Member under that paragraph that was\nin force immediately before the Schedule 1 commencement day\ncontinues to have effect, in relation to the review of the modern\naward, as if that repeal had not happened.\n\nSchedule 1  Application, saving and transitional provisions relating to amendments of\nthis Act",
      "skos:definition": "Scope\n(1) This clause applies in relation to a review of a modern award\nconducted as part of a 4 yearly review of modern awards if:\n(a) the review of the modern award commenced before the\nSchedule 1 commencement day; and\n(b) immediately before that day, the review of the modern award\nhad not been completed.\nSaving\n(2) Despite the repeal of:\n(a) Division 4 of Part 2-3 (which deals with 4 yearly reviews of\nmodern awards); and\n(b) paragraph 582(4)(a) (which deals with directions by the\nPresident); and\n(c) subsections 616(2) and (3) (which deal with the FWC’s\nfunctions etc. that must be performed by a Full Bench);\nby the amending Act, those provisions continue to apply, in\nrelation to the review of the modern award, as if those repeals had\nnot happened.\n(3) Despite the repeal of paragraph 582(4)(a) (which deals with\ndirections by the President) by the amending Act, a direction given\nby the President to an FWC Member under that paragraph that was\nin force immediately before the Schedule 1 commencement day\ncontinues to have effect, in relation to the review of the modern\naward, as if that repeal had not happened.\n\nSchedule 1  Application, saving and transitional provisions relating to amendments of\nthis Act",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:fair-work-act-2009-sch-1-sec-26-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:fair-work-act-2009-sch-1-sec-26-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:fair-work-act-2009-sch-1-sec-26-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "b073f6c68ef8721107fd9815b19b2c35ec111d526b75c2123d1111ba64424000"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/fair-work-act-2009#sch-1-sec-26",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "26 Incomplete review of modern award",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 27,
      "values:originalText": "Scope\n(1) This clause applies in relation to a review of a modern award\nconducted as part of a 4 yearly review of modern awards if:\n(a) the review of the modern award commenced before the\nSchedule 1 commencement day; and\n(b) immediately before that day, the review of the modern award\nhad not been completed.\nSaving\n(2) Despite the repeal of:\n(a) Division 4 of Part 2-3 (which deals with 4 yearly reviews of\nmodern awards); and\n(b) paragraph 582(4)(a) (which deals with directions by the\nPresident); and\n(c) subsections 616(2) and (3) (which deal with the FWC’s\nfunctions etc. that must be performed by a Full Bench);\nby the amending Act, those provisions continue to apply, in\nrelation to the review of the modern award, as if those repeals had\nnot happened.\n(3) Despite the repeal of paragraph 582(4)(a) (which deals with\ndirections by the President) by the amending Act, a direction given\nby the President to an FWC Member under that paragraph that was\nin force immediately before the Schedule 1 commencement day\ncontinues to have effect, in relation to the review of the modern\naward, as if that repeal had not happened.\n\nSchedule 1  Application, saving and transitional provisions relating to amendments of\nthis Act"
    },
