    {
      "@id": "concept:fair-work-act-2009-sch-1-sec-43-ss-4",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "43(4) Amendments about flexible unpaid parental leave",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/fair-work-act-2009#sch-1-sec-43-ss-4"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "fair-work-act-2009.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "fair-work-act-2009.pdf, p.36",
      "values:originalText": "(4) The employee may, in the notice under subclause (2), advise the\nemployer of a change to the end date of the initial leave period, but\nonly if the change is necessary to allow the employee to take the\nflexible unpaid parental leave for the number of days referred to in\nsubclause (3).",
      "skos:definition": "(4) The employee may, in the notice under subclause (2), advise the\nemployer of a change to the end date of the initial leave period, but\nonly if the change is necessary to allow the employee to take the\nflexible unpaid parental leave for the number of days referred to in\nsubclause (3).",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:fair-work-act-2009-sch-1-sec-43"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:fair-work-act-2009-sch-1-sec-43-ss-4-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:fair-work-act-2009-sch-1-sec-43-ss-4-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "1ce6b0d6754de2b48dca7b9a41b5839b2dd2500e533358c9009343c6b145b395",
      "skos:note": "Employee may advise employer of change to leave period end date under certain conditions."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/fair-work-act-2009#sch-1-sec-43-ss-4",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "43(4) Amendments about flexible unpaid parental leave",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 36,
      "values:originalText": "(4) The employee may, in the notice under subclause (2), advise the\nemployer of a change to the end date of the initial leave period, but\nonly if the change is necessary to allow the employee to take the\nflexible unpaid parental leave for the number of days referred to in\nsubclause (3)."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:fair-work-act-2009-sch-1-sec-43-ss-4-norm",
      "@type": "values:Permission",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
