      "cml:premiseText": "(2) Subclause (1) does not apply in relation to a person who is an employee of an employer as a result of accepting an offer that was Schedule 1",
      "cml:conclusionText": "This subclause applies to employees of employers."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:fair-work-act-2009-sch-1-sec-47",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "47 Transitioning casual employees",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/fair-work-act-2009#sch-1-sec-47"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "fair-work-act-2009.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "fair-work-act-2009.pdf, p.41",
      "values:originalText": "(1) This clause applies in relation to an employee and an employer\n(other than a small business employer) if any or all of the following\napply:\n(a) the employee was, immediately before commencement (and\ndisregarding subclause 46(3)), a casual employee of the\nemployer;\n(b) the employee was, immediately before commencement (and\ndisregarding subclause 46(3)), designated as a casual\nemployee by the employer for the purposes of:\n(i) any fair work instrument that applies to the employee;\nor\n(ii) the employee’s contract of employment;\n(c) the employee is a casual employee of the employer within the\nmeaning of section 15A of the amended Act because of an\noffer of an employment made before commencement.\n\nSchedule 1  Application, saving and transitional provisions relating to amendments of\nthis Act",
      "skos:definition": "(1) This clause applies in relation to an employee and an employer\n(other than a small business employer) if any or all of the following\napply:\n(a) the employee was, immediately before commencement (and\ndisregarding subclause 46(3)), a casual employee of the\nemployer;\n(b) the employee was, immediately before commencement (and\ndisregarding subclause 46(3)), designated as a casual\nemployee by the employer for the purposes of:\n(i) any fair work instrument that applies to the employee;\nor\n(ii) the employee’s contract of employment;\n(c) the employee is a casual employee of the employer within the\nmeaning of section 15A of the amended Act because of an\noffer of an employment made before commencement.\n\nSchedule 1  Application, saving and transitional provisions relating to amendments of\nthis Act",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:fair-work-act-2009-sch-1-sec-47-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:fair-work-act-2009-sch-1-sec-47-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "d27a14d8d9a341fd5cfa4c0010e91cf04aab23f47db38211d3e22758020328b6",
      "skos:note": "Employee must be designated as casual employee before commencement."
    },
    {
