    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:fair-work-act-2009-sch-1-sec-53",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "53 Resolving interactions between enterprise agreements and paid",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/fair-work-act-2009#sch-1-sec-53"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "fair-work-act-2009.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "fair-work-act-2009.pdf, p.49",
      "values:originalText": "family and domestic violence leave\n(1) On application by an employer, employee or employee\norganisation covered by a pre-commencement enterprise\nagreement, if:\n(a) the agreement includes terms entitling employees to paid\nfamily and domestic violence leave within the ordinary\nmeaning of that expression; and\n(b) the FWC considers that the effect of those terms is\ndetrimental when compared with the entitlement under\nSubdivision CA of Division 7 of Part 2-2 as amended by\nSchedule 1 to the amending Act (the NES entitlement);\nthe FWC may make a determination varying the agreement to\nmake the agreement consistent with the NES entitlement.\n(2) On application by an employer, employee or employee\norganisation covered by a pre-commencement enterprise\nagreement, the FWC may make a determination varying the\nagreement to make it operate effectively with the following:\n(a) the provisions of Subdivision CA of Division 7 of Part 2-2 as\namended by Schedule 1 to the amending Act;\n(b) section 107, to the extent that it relates to taking leave under\nthat Subdivision.\n(3) A variation of a pre-commencement enterprise agreement under\nthis clause operates from the day specified in the determination,\nwhich may be a day before the determination is made.",
      "skos:definition": "family and domestic violence leave\n(1) On application by an employer, employee or employee\norganisation covered by a pre-commencement enterprise\nagreement, if:\n(a) the agreement includes terms entitling employees to paid\nfamily and domestic violence leave within the ordinary\nmeaning of that expression; and\n(b) the FWC considers that the effect of those terms is\ndetrimental when compared with the entitlement under\nSubdivision CA of Division 7 of Part 2-2 as amended by\nSchedule 1 to the amending Act (the NES entitlement);\nthe FWC may make a determination varying the agreement to\nmake the agreement consistent with the NES entitlement.\n(2) On application by an employer, employee or employee\norganisation covered by a pre-commencement enterprise\nagreement, the FWC may make a determination varying the\nagreement to make it operate effectively with the following:\n(a) the provisions of Subdivision CA of Division 7 of Part 2-2 as\namended by Schedule 1 to the amending Act;\n(b) section 107, to the extent that it relates to taking leave under\nthat Subdivision.\n(3) A variation of a pre-commencement enterprise agreement under\nthis clause operates from the day specified in the determination,\nwhich may be a day before the determination is made.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:fair-work-act-2009-sch-1-sec-53-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:fair-work-act-2009-sch-1-sec-53-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:fair-work-act-2009-sch-1-sec-53-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "5e2974e94930d5cdd1b49756d3848ec5fd5aa71da6e811b57dbca0698aa38c18"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/fair-work-act-2009#sch-1-sec-53",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "53 Resolving interactions between enterprise agreements and paid",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 49,
      "values:originalText": "family and domestic violence leave\n(1) On application by an employer, employee or employee\norganisation covered by a pre-commencement enterprise\nagreement, if:\n(a) the agreement includes terms entitling employees to paid\nfamily and domestic violence leave within the ordinary\nmeaning of that expression; and\n(b) the FWC considers that the effect of those terms is\ndetrimental when compared with the entitlement under\nSubdivision CA of Division 7 of Part 2-2 as amended by\nSchedule 1 to the amending Act (the NES entitlement);\nthe FWC may make a determination varying the agreement to\nmake the agreement consistent with the NES entitlement.\n(2) On application by an employer, employee or employee\norganisation covered by a pre-commencement enterprise\nagreement, the FWC may make a determination varying the\nagreement to make it operate effectively with the following:\n(a) the provisions of Subdivision CA of Division 7 of Part 2-2 as\namended by Schedule 1 to the amending Act;\n(b) section 107, to the extent that it relates to taking leave under\nthat Subdivision.\n(3) A variation of a pre-commencement enterprise agreement under\nthis clause operates from the day specified in the determination,\nwhich may be a day before the determination is made."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:fair-work-act-2009-sch-1-sec-53-ss-1",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "53(1) Resolving interactions between enterprise agreements and paid",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/fair-work-act-2009#sch-1-sec-53-ss-1"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
