    {
      "@id": "concept:fair-work-act-2009-sch-1-sec-58",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "58 Equal remuneration",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/fair-work-act-2009#sch-1-sec-58"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "fair-work-act-2009.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "fair-work-act-2009.pdf, p.54",
      "values:originalText": "(1) Section 157 of the amended Act applies after commencement in\nrelation to a determination or modern award made under that\nsection after commencement.\n(2) Subsections 302(3A) to (4A) of the amended Act apply after\ncommencement in relation to the FWC performing functions, or\nexercising powers, in relation to:\n(a) a matter that arises after commencement; or\n(b) a proceeding in the FWC that was on foot at commencement,\nor commences after commencement.\n(3) If an application under subsection 302(3) of this Act as in force\nimmediately before commencement has not been finally\ndetermined at commencement, subsection 302(5) of the amended\nAct applies in relation to the application as if it were an application\nunder paragraph 302(3)(b) of the amended Act.\n\nApplication, saving and transitional provisions relating to amendments of this Act\nSchedule 1\nAmendments made by the Fair Work Legislation Amendment (Secure Jobs, Better Pay)\nAct 2022  Part 13\nAmendments made by Part 7 of Schedule 1 to the amending Act  Division 5\nClause 59\nFair Work Act 2009\nCompilation date: 02/04/2026",
      "skos:definition": "(1) Section 157 of the amended Act applies after commencement in\nrelation to a determination or modern award made under that\nsection after commencement.\n(2) Subsections 302(3A) to (4A) of the amended Act apply after\ncommencement in relation to the FWC performing functions, or\nexercising powers, in relation to:\n(a) a matter that arises after commencement; or\n(b) a proceeding in the FWC that was on foot at commencement,\nor commences after commencement.\n(3) If an application under subsection 302(3) of this Act as in force\nimmediately before commencement has not been finally\ndetermined at commencement, subsection 302(5) of the amended\nAct applies in relation to the application as if it were an application\nunder paragraph 302(3)(b) of the amended Act.\n\nApplication, saving and transitional provisions relating to amendments of this Act\nSchedule 1\nAmendments made by the Fair Work Legislation Amendment (Secure Jobs, Better Pay)\nAct 2022  Part 13\nAmendments made by Part 7 of Schedule 1 to the amending Act  Division 5\nClause 59\nFair Work Act 2009\nCompilation date: 02/04/2026",
      "cml:hasPart": [
