    {
      "@id": "concept:fair-work-act-2009-sch-1-sec-60",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "60 Prohibiting sexual harassment in connection with work",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/fair-work-act-2009#sch-1-sec-60"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "fair-work-act-2009.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "fair-work-act-2009.pdf, p.57",
      "values:originalText": "(1) Despite the amendments of Part 6-4B made by Schedule 1 to the\namending Act, that Part, as in force immediately before the\ncommencement of Division 1 of Part 8 of that Schedule, continues\nto apply, on and after that commencement, in relation to:\n(a) the sexual harassment of a worker at work before that\ncommencement; and\n(b) the sexual harassment of a worker at work on or after that\ncommencement, if the sexual harassment is part of a course\nof conduct that begins before that commencement.\n(2) Despite the repeal of subsection 789FF(1) by Schedule 1 to the\namending Act, an order that was in force under that subsection\nimmediately before the commencement of Division 1 of Part 8 of\nthat Schedule continues in force (and may be dealt with) on and\nafter that commencement as if that repeal had not happened.\n(3) Subsection 527D(1) does not apply in relation to sexual harassment\nof a worker if the sexual harassment is part of a course of conduct\nthat begins before the commencement of Division 1 of Part 8 of\nSchedule 1 to the amending Act.\n\nSchedule 1  Application, saving and transitional provisions relating to amendments of\nthis Act",
      "skos:definition": "(1) Despite the amendments of Part 6-4B made by Schedule 1 to the\namending Act, that Part, as in force immediately before the\ncommencement of Division 1 of Part 8 of that Schedule, continues\nto apply, on and after that commencement, in relation to:\n(a) the sexual harassment of a worker at work before that\ncommencement; and\n(b) the sexual harassment of a worker at work on or after that\ncommencement, if the sexual harassment is part of a course\nof conduct that begins before that commencement.\n(2) Despite the repeal of subsection 789FF(1) by Schedule 1 to the\namending Act, an order that was in force under that subsection\nimmediately before the commencement of Division 1 of Part 8 of\nthat Schedule continues in force (and may be dealt with) on and\nafter that commencement as if that repeal had not happened.\n(3) Subsection 527D(1) does not apply in relation to sexual harassment\nof a worker if the sexual harassment is part of a course of conduct\nthat begins before the commencement of Division 1 of Part 8 of\nSchedule 1 to the amending Act.\n\nSchedule 1  Application, saving and transitional provisions relating to amendments of\nthis Act",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:fair-work-act-2009-sch-1-sec-60-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:fair-work-act-2009-sch-1-sec-60-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:fair-work-act-2009-sch-1-sec-60-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "d1a34e0202a7bab49a70704df3ce457ea48ce7af8ada2c13a299749a8465dfd3"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/fair-work-act-2009#sch-1-sec-60",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "60 Prohibiting sexual harassment in connection with work",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 57,
      "values:originalText": "(1) Despite the amendments of Part 6-4B made by Schedule 1 to the\namending Act, that Part, as in force immediately before the\ncommencement of Division 1 of Part 8 of that Schedule, continues\nto apply, on and after that commencement, in relation to:\n(a) the sexual harassment of a worker at work before that\ncommencement; and\n(b) the sexual harassment of a worker at work on or after that\ncommencement, if the sexual harassment is part of a course\nof conduct that begins before that commencement.\n(2) Despite the repeal of subsection 789FF(1) by Schedule 1 to the\namending Act, an order that was in force under that subsection\nimmediately before the commencement of Division 1 of Part 8 of\nthat Schedule continues in force (and may be dealt with) on and\nafter that commencement as if that repeal had not happened.\n(3) Subsection 527D(1) does not apply in relation to sexual harassment\nof a worker if the sexual harassment is part of a course of conduct\nthat begins before the commencement of Division 1 of Part 8 of\nSchedule 1 to the amending Act.\n\nSchedule 1  Application, saving and transitional provisions relating to amendments of\nthis Act"
    },
