      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:fair-work-act-2009-sch-1-sec-65",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "65 Termination of enterprise agreements after nominal expiry date",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/fair-work-act-2009#sch-1-sec-65"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "fair-work-act-2009.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "fair-work-act-2009.pdf, p.61",
      "values:originalText": "The amendments made by Part 12 of Schedule 1 to the amending\nAct apply in relation to an application for the termination of an\nenterprise agreement made under section 225:\n(a) on or after the commencement of that Part; or\n(b) before the commencement of that Part if, at that\ncommencement, the FWC has neither terminated nor refused\nto terminate the agreement.\n\nSchedule 1  Application, saving and transitional provisions relating to amendments of\nthis Act",
      "skos:definition": "The amendments made by Part 12 of Schedule 1 to the amending\nAct apply in relation to an application for the termination of an\nenterprise agreement made under section 225:\n(a) on or after the commencement of that Part; or\n(b) before the commencement of that Part if, at that\ncommencement, the FWC has neither terminated nor refused\nto terminate the agreement.\n\nSchedule 1  Application, saving and transitional provisions relating to amendments of\nthis Act",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:fair-work-act-2009-sch-1-sec-65-norm"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "3127cd6764c3112acadcf5c5c824a52eb847c476312a19914c088d8eba9c1ccb",
      "skos:note": "Amendments apply to termination applications made under section 225"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/fair-work-act-2009#sch-1-sec-65",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "65 Termination of enterprise agreements after nominal expiry date",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 61,
      "values:originalText": "The amendments made by Part 12 of Schedule 1 to the amending\nAct apply in relation to an application for the termination of an\nenterprise agreement made under section 225:\n(a) on or after the commencement of that Part; or\n(b) before the commencement of that Part if, at that\ncommencement, the FWC has neither terminated nor refused\nto terminate the agreement.\n\nSchedule 1  Application, saving and transitional provisions relating to amendments of\nthis Act"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:fair-work-act-2009-sch-1-sec-65-norm",
      "@type": "values:Undertaking",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:fair-work-act-2009-sch-1-sec-65"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:fair-work-act-2009-sch-1-sec-66",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "66 Genuine agreement in relation to enterprise agreements",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/fair-work-act-2009#sch-1-sec-66"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "fair-work-act-2009.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "fair-work-act-2009.pdf, p.62",
      "values:originalText": "Despite the amendments made by Part 14 of Schedule 1 to the\namending Act, Part 2-4 continues to apply, as if the amendments\nhad not been made, in relation to:\n(a) any proposed enterprise agreement for which the notification\ntime occurs before the commencement of Part 14 of that\nSchedule; and\n(b) any variation of an enterprise agreement for which the\nemployer’s request that affected employees for the variation\napprove the variation by voting for it occurs before that\ncommencement.\n\nApplication, saving and transitional provisions relating to amendments of this Act\nSchedule 1\nAmendments made by the Fair Work Legislation Amendment (Secure Jobs, Better Pay)\nAct 2022  Part 13\nAmendments made by Part 16 of Schedule 1 to the amending Act  Division 12\nClause 67\nFair Work Act 2009\nCompilation date: 02/04/2026",
      "skos:definition": "Despite the amendments made by Part 14 of Schedule 1 to the\namending Act, Part 2-4 continues to apply, as if the amendments\nhad not been made, in relation to:\n(a) any proposed enterprise agreement for which the notification\ntime occurs before the commencement of Part 14 of that\nSchedule; and\n(b) any variation of an enterprise agreement for which the\nemployer’s request that affected employees for the variation\napprove the variation by voting for it occurs before that\ncommencement.\n\nApplication, saving and transitional provisions relating to amendments of this Act\nSchedule 1\nAmendments made by the Fair Work Legislation Amendment (Secure Jobs, Better Pay)\nAct 2022  Part 13\nAmendments made by Part 16 of Schedule 1 to the amending Act  Division 12\nClause 67\nFair Work Act 2009\nCompilation date: 02/04/2026",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:fair-work-act-2009-sch-1-sec-66-norm"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "907ef5a8f85fdc92d337ed8e18fe8950509de493278218e485754f92e4391f26",
      "skos:note": "Continues application of Part 2-4 despite amendments made by Part 14 of Schedule 1."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/fair-work-act-2009#sch-1-sec-66",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "66 Genuine agreement in relation to enterprise agreements",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 62,
      "values:originalText": "Despite the amendments made by Part 14 of Schedule 1 to the\namending Act, Part 2-4 continues to apply, as if the amendments\nhad not been made, in relation to:\n(a) any proposed enterprise agreement for which the notification\ntime occurs before the commencement of Part 14 of that\nSchedule; and\n(b) any variation of an enterprise agreement for which the\nemployer’s request that affected employees for the variation\napprove the variation by voting for it occurs before that\ncommencement.\n\nApplication, saving and transitional provisions relating to amendments of this Act\nSchedule 1\nAmendments made by the Fair Work Legislation Amendment (Secure Jobs, Better Pay)\nAct 2022  Part 13\nAmendments made by Part 16 of Schedule 1 to the amending Act  Division 12\nClause 67\nFair Work Act 2009\nCompilation date: 02/04/2026"
    },
    {
