    {
      "@id": "concept:fair-work-act-2009-sch-1-sec-72-ss-6",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "72(6) Industrial action",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/fair-work-act-2009#sch-1-sec-72-ss-6"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "fair-work-act-2009.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "fair-work-act-2009.pdf, p.66",
      "values:originalText": "(6) The amendments of Part 3-3 made by Division 4 of Part 19 of\nSchedule 1 to the amending Act apply in relation to employee\nclaim action if the application for the relevant protected action\nballot order is made under subsection 437(1) of this Act on or after\nthe commencement of that Division.",
      "skos:definition": "(6) The amendments of Part 3-3 made by Division 4 of Part 19 of\nSchedule 1 to the amending Act apply in relation to employee\nclaim action if the application for the relevant protected action\nballot order is made under subsection 437(1) of this Act on or after\nthe commencement of that Division.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:fair-work-act-2009-sch-1-sec-72"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:fair-work-act-2009-sch-1-sec-72-ss-6-norm"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "6a8d97a328bdb8e3fe92e96076e980f56d246dfc9bf0b6917fe3f35a49be6418",
      "skos:note": "Conditional commencement of amendments for employee claim actions"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/fair-work-act-2009#sch-1-sec-72-ss-6",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "72(6) Industrial action",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 66,
      "values:originalText": "(6) The amendments of Part 3-3 made by Division 4 of Part 19 of\nSchedule 1 to the amending Act apply in relation to employee\nclaim action if the application for the relevant protected action\nballot order is made under subsection 437(1) of this Act on or after\nthe commencement of that Division."
    },
    {
