      "dc:source": "fair-work-act-2009.pdf, p.78",
      "values:originalText": "then:\n(c) the employee may give the employer a written notice (an\namendment notice) that makes amendments to the\nsubsection 74(1) notice that are consistent with the amended\nAct; and\n(d) if the employee gives an amendment notice to the employer\nin relation to the child:\n(i) the amendments made by the amendment notice must\nnot take effect until at least 4 weeks after the\namendment notice is given to the employer; and\n(ii) any requirement imposed by this Act (other than\nsubsection 74(4) or (4B)) in relation to the period within\nwhich the employer is to be given written notice of the\ntaking of unpaid parental leave is waived for the taking\nof the unpaid parental leave covered by the amendment\nnotice; and\n(e) the employee is not entitled to give more than one\namendment notice to the employer in relation to the child.\n\nApplication, saving and transitional provisions relating to amendments of this Act\nSchedule 1\nAmendments made by the Fair Work Legislation Amendment (Protecting Worker\nEntitlements) Act 2023  Part 14\nAmendments made by Schedule 3 to the amending Act  Division 3\nClause 88\nFair Work Act 2009\nCompilation date: 02/04/2026",
      "skos:definition": "then:\n(c) the employee may give the employer a written notice (an\namendment notice) that makes amendments to the\nsubsection 74(1) notice that are consistent with the amended\nAct; and\n(d) if the employee gives an amendment notice to the employer\nin relation to the child:\n(i) the amendments made by the amendment notice must\nnot take effect until at least 4 weeks after the\namendment notice is given to the employer; and\n(ii) any requirement imposed by this Act (other than\nsubsection 74(4) or (4B)) in relation to the period within\nwhich the employer is to be given written notice of the\ntaking of unpaid parental leave is waived for the taking\nof the unpaid parental leave covered by the amendment\nnotice; and\n(e) the employee is not entitled to give more than one\namendment notice to the employer in relation to the child.\n\nApplication, saving and transitional provisions relating to amendments of this Act\nSchedule 1\nAmendments made by the Fair Work Legislation Amendment (Protecting Worker\nEntitlements) Act 2023  Part 14\nAmendments made by Schedule 3 to the amending Act  Division 3\nClause 88\nFair Work Act 2009\nCompilation date: 02/04/2026",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:fair-work-act-2009-sch-1-sec-1-5-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:fair-work-act-2009-sch-1-sec-1-5-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "70ec9d692eb8105770e4a91b212fd7fc91f10f6c26c7f51717a662cff9e9a2d7",
      "skos:note": "Employee may give employer a written notice to make amendments to subsection 74(1) notice."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/fair-work-act-2009#sch-1-sec-1-5",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "1 July 2023;",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 78,
      "values:originalText": "then:\n(c) the employee may give the employer a written notice (an\namendment notice) that makes amendments to the\nsubsection 74(1) notice that are consistent with the amended\nAct; and\n(d) if the employee gives an amendment notice to the employer\nin relation to the child:\n(i) the amendments made by the amendment notice must\nnot take effect until at least 4 weeks after the\namendment notice is given to the employer; and\n(ii) any requirement imposed by this Act (other than\nsubsection 74(4) or (4B)) in relation to the period within\nwhich the employer is to be given written notice of the\ntaking of unpaid parental leave is waived for the taking\nof the unpaid parental leave covered by the amendment\nnotice; and\n(e) the employee is not entitled to give more than one\namendment notice to the employer in relation to the child.\n\nApplication, saving and transitional provisions relating to amendments of this Act\nSchedule 1\nAmendments made by the Fair Work Legislation Amendment (Protecting Worker\nEntitlements) Act 2023  Part 14\nAmendments made by Schedule 3 to the amending Act  Division 3\nClause 88\nFair Work Act 2009\nCompilation date: 02/04/2026"
    },
