      },
      "dc:source": "fair-work-act-2009.pdf, p.89",
      "values:originalText": "In this Part:\namended Act means this Act as amended by the Fair Work\nLegislation Amendment (Closing Loopholes No. 2) Act 2024.\namending Act means the Fair Work Legislation Amendment\n(Closing Loopholes No. 2) Act 2024.\n\nSchedule 1  Application, saving and transitional provisions relating to amendments of\nthis Act",
      "skos:definition": "In this Part:\namended Act means this Act as amended by the Fair Work\nLegislation Amendment (Closing Loopholes No. 2) Act 2024.\namending Act means the Fair Work Legislation Amendment\n(Closing Loopholes No. 2) Act 2024.\n\nSchedule 1  Application, saving and transitional provisions relating to amendments of\nthis Act",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:fair-work-act-2009-sch-1-sec-100-norm"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "2b4f515a2c430af4cb266b279b39ab4d0b640aeb529496a8abb2235249e840db",
      "skos:note": "Definitions for amended and namending Acts"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/fair-work-act-2009#sch-1-sec-100",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "100 Definitions",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 89,
      "values:originalText": "In this Part:\namended Act means this Act as amended by the Fair Work\nLegislation Amendment (Closing Loopholes No. 2) Act 2024.\namending Act means the Fair Work Legislation Amendment\n(Closing Loopholes No. 2) Act 2024.\n\nSchedule 1  Application, saving and transitional provisions relating to amendments of\nthis Act"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:fair-work-act-2009-sch-1-sec-100-norm",
      "@type": "values:Undertaking",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:fair-work-act-2009-sch-1-sec-100"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:fair-work-act-2009-sch-1-sec-101",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "101 Resolving uncertainties and difficulties about interaction",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/fair-work-act-2009#sch-1-sec-101"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "fair-work-act-2009.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "fair-work-act-2009.pdf, p.90",
      "values:originalText": "between fair work instruments and the definition of\ncasual employee and employee choice\n(1) The FWC may make a determination varying a fair work\ninstrument that is a modern award, enterprise agreement or\nworkplace determination that was made before the commencement\nof this clause:\n(a) for an enterprise agreement or workplace determination—on\napplication by an employer, employee or employee\norganisation covered by the enterprise agreement or\nworkplace determination; or\n(b) for a modern award:\n(i) by the FWC on its own initiative; or\n(ii) on application by an employer organisation or employee\norganisation entitled to represent the industrial interests\nof an employer or employee covered by the award.\n(2) The FWC may make a determination varying the instrument:\n(a) to resolve an uncertainty or difficulty relating to the\ninteraction between the instrument and any of the following:\n(i) the definition of casual employee in section 15A of the\namended Act (including to deal with uncertainty or\ndifficulty arising from the circumstances in which\nemployees are to be employed as casual employees\nunder the agreement);\n(ii) the provisions of Division 4A of Part 2-2 of the\namended Act; or\n(b) to make the instrument operate effectively with that section\nor those provisions.\n\nApplication, saving and transitional provisions relating to amendments of this Act\nSchedule 1\nMain amendments made by the Fair Work Legislation Amendment (Closing Loopholes\nNo. 2) Act 2024  Part 16\nAmendments made by Part 1 of Schedule 1 to the amending Act  Division 2\nClause 102\nFair Work Act 2009\nCompilation date: 02/04/2026\n(3) A variation of a fair work instrument under this clause operates\nfrom the day specified in the determination, which may be a day\nbefore the determination is made.\n(4) If the determination relates to a modern award, the FWC must\npublish the award as varied as soon as practicable on the FWC’s\nwebsite or by any other means the FWC considers appropriate.",
      "skos:definition": "between fair work instruments and the definition of\ncasual employee and employee choice\n(1) The FWC may make a determination varying a fair work\ninstrument that is a modern award, enterprise agreement or\nworkplace determination that was made before the commencement\nof this clause:\n(a) for an enterprise agreement or workplace determination—on\napplication by an employer, employee or employee\norganisation covered by the enterprise agreement or\nworkplace determination; or\n(b) for a modern award:\n(i) by the FWC on its own initiative; or\n(ii) on application by an employer organisation or employee\norganisation entitled to represent the industrial interests\nof an employer or employee covered by the award.\n(2) The FWC may make a determination varying the instrument:\n(a) to resolve an uncertainty or difficulty relating to the\ninteraction between the instrument and any of the following:\n(i) the definition of casual employee in section 15A of the\namended Act (including to deal with uncertainty or\ndifficulty arising from the circumstances in which\nemployees are to be employed as casual employees\nunder the agreement);\n(ii) the provisions of Division 4A of Part 2-2 of the\namended Act; or\n(b) to make the instrument operate effectively with that section\nor those provisions.\n\nApplication, saving and transitional provisions relating to amendments of this Act\nSchedule 1\nMain amendments made by the Fair Work Legislation Amendment (Closing Loopholes\nNo. 2) Act 2024  Part 16\nAmendments made by Part 1 of Schedule 1 to the amending Act  Division 2\nClause 102\nFair Work Act 2009\nCompilation date: 02/04/2026\n(3) A variation of a fair work instrument under this clause operates\nfrom the day specified in the determination, which may be a day\nbefore the determination is made.\n(4) If the determination relates to a modern award, the FWC must\npublish the award as varied as soon as practicable on the FWC’s\nwebsite or by any other means the FWC considers appropriate.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:fair-work-act-2009-sch-1-sec-101-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:fair-work-act-2009-sch-1-sec-101-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:fair-work-act-2009-sch-1-sec-101-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:fair-work-act-2009-sch-1-sec-101-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "c1a03761271a3c3271646ea4dd3091901db5445eb35d4591a20d8fffe58596ca"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/fair-work-act-2009#sch-1-sec-101",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "101 Resolving uncertainties and difficulties about interaction",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 90,
      "values:originalText": "between fair work instruments and the definition of\ncasual employee and employee choice\n(1) The FWC may make a determination varying a fair work\ninstrument that is a modern award, enterprise agreement or\nworkplace determination that was made before the commencement\nof this clause:\n(a) for an enterprise agreement or workplace determination—on\napplication by an employer, employee or employee\norganisation covered by the enterprise agreement or\nworkplace determination; or\n(b) for a modern award:\n(i) by the FWC on its own initiative; or\n(ii) on application by an employer organisation or employee\norganisation entitled to represent the industrial interests\nof an employer or employee covered by the award.\n(2) The FWC may make a determination varying the instrument:\n(a) to resolve an uncertainty or difficulty relating to the\ninteraction between the instrument and any of the following:\n(i) the definition of casual employee in section 15A of the\namended Act (including to deal with uncertainty or\ndifficulty arising from the circumstances in which\nemployees are to be employed as casual employees\nunder the agreement);\n(ii) the provisions of Division 4A of Part 2-2 of the\namended Act; or\n(b) to make the instrument operate effectively with that section\nor those provisions.\n\nApplication, saving and transitional provisions relating to amendments of this Act\nSchedule 1\nMain amendments made by the Fair Work Legislation Amendment (Closing Loopholes\nNo. 2) Act 2024  Part 16\nAmendments made by Part 1 of Schedule 1 to the amending Act  Division 2\nClause 102\nFair Work Act 2009\nCompilation date: 02/04/2026\n(3) A variation of a fair work instrument under this clause operates\nfrom the day specified in the determination, which may be a day\nbefore the determination is made.\n(4) If the determination relates to a modern award, the FWC must\npublish the award as varied as soon as practicable on the FWC’s\nwebsite or by any other means the FWC considers appropriate."
    },
