    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/fair-work-act-2009#sch-1-sec-107-ss-1",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "107(1) Model terms and enterprise agreements",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 96,
      "values:originalText": "(1) Despite the amendments made by Part 5 of Schedule 1 to the\namending Act, sections 202, 205 and 737, as in force immediately\nbefore the commencement of that Part, continue to apply in\nrelation to an enterprise agreement if:\n(a) before that commencement, the employer concerned asks the\nemployees to approve the agreement by voting for it; and\n(b) by that vote, the employees approve the agreement; and\n(c) the FWC approves the agreement."
    },
