      },
      "cml:premiseText": "Amendments made by Part 5 of Schedule 1",
      "cml:conclusionText": "Section 768BK continues to apply."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:fair-work-act-2009-sch-1-sec-109",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "109 Disallowance—model terms made before commencement",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/fair-work-act-2009#sch-1-sec-109"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "fair-work-act-2009.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "fair-work-act-2009.pdf, p.96",
      "values:originalText": "Section 42 (disallowance) of the Legislation Act 2003 does not\napply to a determination made in the exercise of a power under\nsubsection 202(5), 205(3), 737(1) or 768BK(1A) of the amended\nAct, before the commencement of Part 5 of Schedule 1 to the\namending Act, relying on subsection 4(1) of the Acts Interpretation\nAct 1901.\n\nApplication, saving and transitional provisions relating to amendments of this Act\nSchedule 1\nMain amendments made by the Fair Work Legislation Amendment (Closing Loopholes\nNo. 2) Act 2024  Part 16\nAmendments made by Part 5 of Schedule 1 to the amending Act  Division 4\nClause 109\nFair Work Act 2009\nCompilation date: 02/04/2026\nNote:\nSubsection 4(1) of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901 provides for the\nexercise of powers between the passing and commencement of an Act.\n\nSchedule 1  Application, saving and transitional provisions relating to amendments of\nthis Act",
      "skos:definition": "Section 42 (disallowance) of the Legislation Act 2003 does not\napply to a determination made in the exercise of a power under\nsubsection 202(5), 205(3), 737(1) or 768BK(1A) of the amended\nAct, before the commencement of Part 5 of Schedule 1 to the\namending Act, relying on subsection 4(1) of the Acts Interpretation\nAct 1901.\n\nApplication, saving and transitional provisions relating to amendments of this Act\nSchedule 1\nMain amendments made by the Fair Work Legislation Amendment (Closing Loopholes\nNo. 2) Act 2024  Part 16\nAmendments made by Part 5 of Schedule 1 to the amending Act  Division 4\nClause 109\nFair Work Act 2009\nCompilation date: 02/04/2026\nNote:\nSubsection 4(1) of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901 provides for the\nexercise of powers between the passing and commencement of an Act.\n\nSchedule 1  Application, saving and transitional provisions relating to amendments of\nthis Act",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:fair-work-act-2009-sch-1-sec-109-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:fair-work-act-2009-sch-1-sec-109-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "ee18007ed69b65c8d8e72729ba8f409b33854c06477b1b9cbbe78bde05dc8ffa",
      "skos:note": "Section 42 of the Legislation Act 2003 does not apply to a determination made in the exercise of certain powers."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/fair-work-act-2009#sch-1-sec-109",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "109 Disallowance—model terms made before commencement",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 96,
      "values:originalText": "Section 42 (disallowance) of the Legislation Act 2003 does not\napply to a determination made in the exercise of a power under\nsubsection 202(5), 205(3), 737(1) or 768BK(1A) of the amended\nAct, before the commencement of Part 5 of Schedule 1 to the\namending Act, relying on subsection 4(1) of the Acts Interpretation\nAct 1901.\n\nApplication, saving and transitional provisions relating to amendments of this Act\nSchedule 1\nMain amendments made by the Fair Work Legislation Amendment (Closing Loopholes\nNo. 2) Act 2024  Part 16\nAmendments made by Part 5 of Schedule 1 to the amending Act  Division 4\nClause 109\nFair Work Act 2009\nCompilation date: 02/04/2026\nNote:\nSubsection 4(1) of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901 provides for the\nexercise of powers between the passing and commencement of an Act.\n\nSchedule 1  Application, saving and transitional provisions relating to amendments of\nthis Act"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:fair-work-act-2009-sch-1-sec-109-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:fair-work-act-2009-sch-1-sec-109"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:State"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:fair-work-act-2009-sch-1-sec-109-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Exclusion",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Section 42 does not apply to certain determinations.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 0.5,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "Subsection 4(1) of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901 provides for the exercise of powers between the passing and commencement of an Act.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "Section 42 does not apply."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:fair-work-act-2009-sch-1-sec-110",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "110 Application of amendments—intractable bargaining workplace",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/fair-work-act-2009#sch-1-sec-110"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "fair-work-act-2009.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "fair-work-act-2009.pdf, p.98",
      "values:originalText": "determinations\n(1) This clause applies to the following provisions:\n(a) section 270A of the amended Act;\n(b) subsection 274(3) of the amended Act.\n(2) The provisions apply in relation to determinations made on or after\nthe commencement of Part 5A of Schedule 1 to the amending Act\n(including determinations in relation to which the declaration\nconcerned, or the application for the declaration concerned, was\nmade before that commencement).\n(3) The provisions also apply in relation to determinations made\nbefore that commencement, in the circumstances specified in\nclause 111.",
      "skos:definition": "determinations\n(1) This clause applies to the following provisions:\n(a) section 270A of the amended Act;\n(b) subsection 274(3) of the amended Act.\n(2) The provisions apply in relation to determinations made on or after\nthe commencement of Part 5A of Schedule 1 to the amending Act\n(including determinations in relation to which the declaration\nconcerned, or the application for the declaration concerned, was\nmade before that commencement).\n(3) The provisions also apply in relation to determinations made\nbefore that commencement, in the circumstances specified in\nclause 111.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:fair-work-act-2009-sch-1-sec-110-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:fair-work-act-2009-sch-1-sec-110-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:fair-work-act-2009-sch-1-sec-110-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "81b25ffd53c8b123485f6ba8ad7becc05475989d703d8f235d88afe6ee5b712a"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/fair-work-act-2009#sch-1-sec-110",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "110 Application of amendments—intractable bargaining workplace",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 98,
      "values:originalText": "determinations\n(1) This clause applies to the following provisions:\n(a) section 270A of the amended Act;\n(b) subsection 274(3) of the amended Act.\n(2) The provisions apply in relation to determinations made on or after\nthe commencement of Part 5A of Schedule 1 to the amending Act\n(including determinations in relation to which the declaration\nconcerned, or the application for the declaration concerned, was\nmade before that commencement).\n(3) The provisions also apply in relation to determinations made\nbefore that commencement, in the circumstances specified in\nclause 111."
    },
