    {
      "@id": "concept:fair-work-act-2009-sch-1-sec-111",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "111 Application of amendments to intractable bargaining workplace",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/fair-work-act-2009#sch-1-sec-111"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "fair-work-act-2009.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "fair-work-act-2009.pdf, p.98",
      "values:originalText": "determinations made before commencement\n(1) This clause applies in relation to an intractable bargaining\nworkplace determination made before the commencement of\nPart 5A of Schedule 1 to the amending Act (the original\ndetermination).\n(2) On application by an employer, employee or employee\norganisation covered by the original determination, the FWC must\nmake a determination (a variation) varying the original\ndetermination where required so as to give effect to the provisions\nto which clause 110 applies.\n\nApplication, saving and transitional provisions relating to amendments of this Act\nSchedule 1\nMain amendments made by the Fair Work Legislation Amendment (Closing Loopholes\nNo. 2) Act 2024  Part 16\nAmendments made by Part 5A of Schedule 1 to the amending Act  Division 5\nClause 111\nFair Work Act 2009\nCompilation date: 02/04/2026\n(3) An application under subclause (2) must be made before the end of\nthe period of 12 months commencing on the day Part 5A of\nSchedule 1 to the amending Act commences.\n(4) The FWC may make a variation despite paragraph 603(3)(c).\n(5) Any variation must be made by a Full Bench.\n(6) A variation operates from the day specified by the FWC in the\nvariation, which must not be a day before the variation is made.\n\nSchedule 1  Application, saving and transitional provisions relating to amendments of\nthis Act",
      "skos:definition": "determinations made before commencement\n(1) This clause applies in relation to an intractable bargaining\nworkplace determination made before the commencement of\nPart 5A of Schedule 1 to the amending Act (the original\ndetermination).\n(2) On application by an employer, employee or employee\norganisation covered by the original determination, the FWC must\nmake a determination (a variation) varying the original\ndetermination where required so as to give effect to the provisions\nto which clause 110 applies.\n\nApplication, saving and transitional provisions relating to amendments of this Act\nSchedule 1\nMain amendments made by the Fair Work Legislation Amendment (Closing Loopholes\nNo. 2) Act 2024  Part 16\nAmendments made by Part 5A of Schedule 1 to the amending Act  Division 5\nClause 111\nFair Work Act 2009\nCompilation date: 02/04/2026\n(3) An application under subclause (2) must be made before the end of\nthe period of 12 months commencing on the day Part 5A of\nSchedule 1 to the amending Act commences.\n(4) The FWC may make a variation despite paragraph 603(3)(c).\n(5) Any variation must be made by a Full Bench.\n(6) A variation operates from the day specified by the FWC in the\nvariation, which must not be a day before the variation is made.\n\nSchedule 1  Application, saving and transitional provisions relating to amendments of\nthis Act",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:fair-work-act-2009-sch-1-sec-111-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:fair-work-act-2009-sch-1-sec-111-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:fair-work-act-2009-sch-1-sec-111-ss-3"
