    {
      "@id": "concept:fair-work-act-2009-sch-1-sec-116",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "116 Relationships in existence as at commencement or entered into",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/fair-work-act-2009#sch-1-sec-116"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "fair-work-act-2009.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "fair-work-act-2009.pdf, p.106",
      "values:originalText": "on or after commencement\n(1) Subject to this Schedule and sections 15AB to 15AD of the\namended Act, section 15AA of the amended Act applies on and\nafter commencement to the following:\n(a) a relationship between an individual and a person entered\ninto before commencement that is in existence as at\ncommencement;\n(b) a relationship between an individual and a person entered\ninto on or after commencement.\n(2) Despite section 40A, section 7 of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901,\nas in force from time to time, applies in relation to the amendment\nmade by item 237 of Part 15 of Schedule 1 to the amending Act.\nNote:\nSection 7 of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901 provides for the effect of\namendment and repeal of provisions of Acts, including in relation to\nrights, liabilities, penalties and forfeitures etc. accrued or incurred\nbefore the repeal.",
      "skos:definition": "on or after commencement\n(1) Subject to this Schedule and sections 15AB to 15AD of the\namended Act, section 15AA of the amended Act applies on and\nafter commencement to the following:\n(a) a relationship between an individual and a person entered\ninto before commencement that is in existence as at\ncommencement;\n(b) a relationship between an individual and a person entered\ninto on or after commencement.\n(2) Despite section 40A, section 7 of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901,\nas in force from time to time, applies in relation to the amendment\nmade by item 237 of Part 15 of Schedule 1 to the amending Act.\nNote:\nSection 7 of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901 provides for the effect of\namendment and repeal of provisions of Acts, including in relation to\nrights, liabilities, penalties and forfeitures etc. accrued or incurred\nbefore the repeal.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:fair-work-act-2009-sch-1-sec-116-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:fair-work-act-2009-sch-1-sec-116-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "2e06fda06fbc69beae1a56c2c93e99534097b8639f0948f553624e0faded91a3"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/fair-work-act-2009#sch-1-sec-116",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "116 Relationships in existence as at commencement or entered into",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 106,
      "values:originalText": "on or after commencement\n(1) Subject to this Schedule and sections 15AB to 15AD of the\namended Act, section 15AA of the amended Act applies on and\nafter commencement to the following:\n(a) a relationship between an individual and a person entered\ninto before commencement that is in existence as at\ncommencement;\n(b) a relationship between an individual and a person entered\ninto on or after commencement.\n(2) Despite section 40A, section 7 of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901,\nas in force from time to time, applies in relation to the amendment\nmade by item 237 of Part 15 of Schedule 1 to the amending Act.\nNote:\nSection 7 of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901 provides for the effect of\namendment and repeal of provisions of Acts, including in relation to\nrights, liabilities, penalties and forfeitures etc. accrued or incurred\nbefore the repeal."
    },
