    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:fair-work-act-2009-sch-1-sec-117",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "117 References to employees etc. in fair work instruments made",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/fair-work-act-2009#sch-1-sec-117"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "fair-work-act-2009.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "fair-work-act-2009.pdf, p.106",
      "values:originalText": "before commencement\n(1) This clause applies to a fair work instrument that:\n(a) was made before commencement; and\n(b) is in operation on or after commencement.\n(2) A reference in the fair work instrument to an employee or an\nemployer is taken, on and after commencement, to include a\nreference to an employee or an employer, as the case requires,\nwithin the meaning of section 15AA of the amended Act, and, to\navoid doubt, does not include a reference to an individual in\nrespect of whom an opt out notice has been given and not revoked.\n\nApplication, saving and transitional provisions relating to amendments of this Act\nSchedule 1\nAmendments made by Part 15 of Schedule 1 to the Fair Work Legislation Amendment\n(Closing Loopholes No. 2) Act 2024  Part 17\nTransitional provisions  Division 2\nClause 118\nFair Work Act 2009\nCompilation date: 02/04/2026",
      "skos:definition": "before commencement\n(1) This clause applies to a fair work instrument that:\n(a) was made before commencement; and\n(b) is in operation on or after commencement.\n(2) A reference in the fair work instrument to an employee or an\nemployer is taken, on and after commencement, to include a\nreference to an employee or an employer, as the case requires,\nwithin the meaning of section 15AA of the amended Act, and, to\navoid doubt, does not include a reference to an individual in\nrespect of whom an opt out notice has been given and not revoked.\n\nApplication, saving and transitional provisions relating to amendments of this Act\nSchedule 1\nAmendments made by Part 15 of Schedule 1 to the Fair Work Legislation Amendment\n(Closing Loopholes No. 2) Act 2024  Part 17\nTransitional provisions  Division 2\nClause 118\nFair Work Act 2009\nCompilation date: 02/04/2026",
