    {
      "@id": "concept:fair-work-act-2009-sch-1-sec-118",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "118 Entitlements determined by reference to length of a period of",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/fair-work-act-2009#sch-1-sec-118"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "fair-work-act-2009.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "fair-work-act-2009.pdf, p.107",
      "values:originalText": "employment etc.\n(1) This clause applies if:\n(a) immediately before commencement, an individual was not an\nemployee of a person within the ordinary meaning of that\nexpression; and\n(b) because of the operation of section 15AA of the amended\nAct, on commencement, the individual becomes an employee\nof the person, within the ordinary meaning of that expression,\nin respect of that relationship.\n(2) For the purposes of determining whether the individual has a right\nor entitlement under the amended Act or under a fair work\ninstrument in respect of the employment of the individual, being a\nright or entitlement calculated by reference to:\n(a) the individual’s length of service (however described) as an\nemployee; or\n(b) a minimum period of employment (however described) of the\nindividual;\nthe nature of the relationship between the individual and the person\nin respect of a period or periods before commencement is to be\nascertained in accordance with the old Act.",
      "skos:definition": "employment etc.\n(1) This clause applies if:\n(a) immediately before commencement, an individual was not an\nemployee of a person within the ordinary meaning of that\nexpression; and\n(b) because of the operation of section 15AA of the amended\nAct, on commencement, the individual becomes an employee\nof the person, within the ordinary meaning of that expression,\nin respect of that relationship.\n(2) For the purposes of determining whether the individual has a right\nor entitlement under the amended Act or under a fair work\ninstrument in respect of the employment of the individual, being a\nright or entitlement calculated by reference to:\n(a) the individual’s length of service (however described) as an\nemployee; or\n(b) a minimum period of employment (however described) of the\nindividual;\nthe nature of the relationship between the individual and the person\nin respect of a period or periods before commencement is to be\nascertained in accordance with the old Act.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:fair-work-act-2009-sch-1-sec-118-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:fair-work-act-2009-sch-1-sec-118-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "c443bb95ba14564846c668a335b6fc0450b0e0d504aaae9201e2da7a87f53c55"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/fair-work-act-2009#sch-1-sec-118",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "118 Entitlements determined by reference to length of a period of",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 107,
      "values:originalText": "employment etc.\n(1) This clause applies if:\n(a) immediately before commencement, an individual was not an\nemployee of a person within the ordinary meaning of that\nexpression; and\n(b) because of the operation of section 15AA of the amended\nAct, on commencement, the individual becomes an employee\nof the person, within the ordinary meaning of that expression,\nin respect of that relationship.\n(2) For the purposes of determining whether the individual has a right\nor entitlement under the amended Act or under a fair work\ninstrument in respect of the employment of the individual, being a\nright or entitlement calculated by reference to:\n(a) the individual’s length of service (however described) as an\nemployee; or\n(b) a minimum period of employment (however described) of the\nindividual;\nthe nature of the relationship between the individual and the person\nin respect of a period or periods before commencement is to be\nascertained in accordance with the old Act."
    },
