      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:fair-work-act-2009-sch-1-sec-120",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "120 FWC power to deal with uncertainties or difficulties arising",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/fair-work-act-2009#sch-1-sec-120"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "fair-work-act-2009.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "fair-work-act-2009.pdf, p.108",
      "values:originalText": "from the operation of section 15AA of the amended Act\n(1) The FWC may make a determination varying a fair work\ninstrument in order to resolve an uncertainty or difficulty relating\nto the operation or effect of the fair work instrument, being an\nuncertainty or difficulty arising as a result of, or in connection\nwith, the amendment made by item 237 of Part 15 of Schedule 1 to\nthe amending Act.\n(2) The FWC may make a determination under subclause (1) varying a\nmodern award:\n(a) on its own initiative; or\n(b) on application by an employer, employee, organisation or\noutworker entity covered by the modern award; or\n(c) on application by an organisation that is entitled to represent\nthe industrial interests of one or more employers or\nemployees covered by the modern award; or\n(d) if the modern award includes outworker terms—on\napplication by an organisation that is entitled to represent the\nindustrial interests of one or more outworkers to whom the\noutworker terms relate.\n(3) The FWC may make a determination under subclause (1) varying\nan enterprise agreement or a workplace determination:\n(a) on its own initiative; or\n(b) on application by any of the following:\n(i) one or more of the employers covered by the enterprise\nagreement or workplace determination;\n\nApplication, saving and transitional provisions relating to amendments of this Act\nSchedule 1\nAmendments made by Part 15 of Schedule 1 to the Fair Work Legislation Amendment\n(Closing Loopholes No. 2) Act 2024  Part 17\nTransitional provisions  Division 2\nClause 120\nFair Work Act 2009\nCompilation date: 02/04/2026\n(ii) an employee covered by the enterprise agreement or\nworkplace determination;\n(iii) an employee organisation covered by the enterprise\nagreement or workplace determination.\n(4) The FWC may make a determination under subclause (1) varying\nan FWC order:\n(a) on its own initiative; or\n(b) on application:\n(i) by a person affected by the order; or\n(ii) if the FWC order is of a kind prescribed by the\nregulations—by a person prescribed by the regulations\nin relation to that kind of order.\n(5) A variation of a fair work instrument under this clause operates\nfrom the day specified in the determination, which may be a day\nbefore the determination was made.\n(6) The regulations may provide as follows:\n(a) that this clause applies, or does not apply, to a specified fair\nwork instrument or a specified class of fair work instrument;\n(b) that this clause applies, or does not apply, to a specified\nuncertainty or difficulty, or a specified class of uncertainty or\ndifficulty.\n\nSchedule 1  Application, saving and transitional provisions relating to amendments of\nthis Act",
      "skos:definition": "from the operation of section 15AA of the amended Act\n(1) The FWC may make a determination varying a fair work\ninstrument in order to resolve an uncertainty or difficulty relating\nto the operation or effect of the fair work instrument, being an\nuncertainty or difficulty arising as a result of, or in connection\nwith, the amendment made by item 237 of Part 15 of Schedule 1 to\nthe amending Act.\n(2) The FWC may make a determination under subclause (1) varying a\nmodern award:\n(a) on its own initiative; or\n(b) on application by an employer, employee, organisation or\noutworker entity covered by the modern award; or\n(c) on application by an organisation that is entitled to represent\nthe industrial interests of one or more employers or\nemployees covered by the modern award; or\n(d) if the modern award includes outworker terms—on\napplication by an organisation that is entitled to represent the\nindustrial interests of one or more outworkers to whom the\noutworker terms relate.\n(3) The FWC may make a determination under subclause (1) varying\nan enterprise agreement or a workplace determination:\n(a) on its own initiative; or\n(b) on application by any of the following:\n(i) one or more of the employers covered by the enterprise\nagreement or workplace determination;\n\nApplication, saving and transitional provisions relating to amendments of this Act\nSchedule 1\nAmendments made by Part 15 of Schedule 1 to the Fair Work Legislation Amendment\n(Closing Loopholes No. 2) Act 2024  Part 17\nTransitional provisions  Division 2\nClause 120\nFair Work Act 2009\nCompilation date: 02/04/2026\n(ii) an employee covered by the enterprise agreement or\nworkplace determination;\n(iii) an employee organisation covered by the enterprise\nagreement or workplace determination.\n(4) The FWC may make a determination under subclause (1) varying\nan FWC order:\n(a) on its own initiative; or\n(b) on application:\n(i) by a person affected by the order; or\n(ii) if the FWC order is of a kind prescribed by the\nregulations—by a ",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:fair-work-act-2009-sch-1-sec-120-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:fair-work-act-2009-sch-1-sec-120-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:fair-work-act-2009-sch-1-sec-120-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:fair-work-act-2009-sch-1-sec-120-ss-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:fair-work-act-2009-sch-1-sec-120-ss-5"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:fair-work-act-2009-sch-1-sec-120-ss-6"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "7186076eab6151c7d4fecdd73385dd8aa57bef77cb90bce3b7e4968cfa80ce49"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/fair-work-act-2009#sch-1-sec-120",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "120 FWC power to deal with uncertainties or difficulties arising",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 108,
      "values:originalText": "from the operation of section 15AA of the amended Act\n(1) The FWC may make a determination varying a fair work\ninstrument in order to resolve an uncertainty or difficulty relating\nto the operation or effect of the fair work instrument, being an\nuncertainty or difficulty arising as a result of, or in connection\nwith, the amendment made by item 237 of Part 15 of Schedule 1 to\nthe amending Act.\n(2) The FWC may make a determination under subclause (1) varying a\nmodern award:\n(a) on its own initiative; or\n(b) on application by an employer, employee, organisation or\noutworker entity covered by the modern award; or\n(c) on application by an organisation that is entitled to represent\nthe industrial interests of one or more employers or\nemployees covered by the modern award; or\n(d) if the modern award includes outworker terms—on\napplication by an organisation that is entitled to represent the\nindustrial interests of one or more outworkers to whom the\noutworker terms relate.\n(3) The FWC may make a determination under subclause (1) varying\nan enterprise agreement or a workplace determination:\n(a) on its own initiative; or\n(b) on application by any of the following:\n(i) one or more of the employers covered by the enterprise\nagreement or workplace determination;\n\nApplication, saving and transitional provisions relating to amendments of this Act\nSchedule 1\nAmendments made by Part 15 of Schedule 1 to the Fair Work Legislation Amendment\n(Closing Loopholes No. 2) Act 2024  Part 17\nTransitional provisions  Division 2\nClause 120\nFair Work Act 2009\nCompilation date: 02/04/2026\n(ii) an employee covered by the enterprise agreement or\nworkplace determination;\n(iii) an employee organisation covered by the enterprise\nagreement or workplace determination.\n(4) The FWC may make a determination under subclause (1) varying\nan FWC order:\n(a) on its own initiative; or\n(b) on application:\n(i) by a person affected by the order; or\n(ii) if the FWC order is of a kind prescribed by the\nregulations—by a person prescribed by the regulations\nin relation to that kind of order.\n(5) A variation of a fair work instrument under this clause operates\nfrom the day specified in the determination, which may be a day\nbefore the determination was made.\n(6) The regulations may provide as follows:\n(a) that this clause applies, or does not apply, to a specified fair\nwork instrument or a specified class of fair work instrument;\n(b) that this clause applies, or does not apply, to a specified\nuncertainty or difficulty, or a specified class of uncertainty or\ndifficulty.\n\nSchedule 1  Application, saving and transitional provisions relating to amendments of\nthis Act"
    },
    {
