    {
      "@id": "concept:fair-work-act-2009-sch-1-sec-120-ss-3",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "120(3) FWC power to deal with uncertainties or difficulties arising",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/fair-work-act-2009#sch-1-sec-120-ss-3"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "fair-work-act-2009.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "fair-work-act-2009.pdf, p.108",
      "values:originalText": "(3) The FWC may make a determination under subclause (1) varying\nan enterprise agreement or a workplace determination:\n(a) on its own initiative; or\n(b) on application by any of the following:\n(i) one or more of the employers covered by the enterprise\nagreement or workplace determination;\n\nApplication, saving and transitional provisions relating to amendments of this Act\nSchedule 1\nAmendments made by Part 15 of Schedule 1 to the Fair Work Legislation Amendment\n(Closing Loopholes No. 2) Act 2024  Part 17\nTransitional provisions  Division 2\nClause 120\nFair Work Act 2009\nCompilation date: 02/04/2026\n(ii) an employee covered by the enterprise agreement or\nworkplace determination;\n(iii) an employee organisation covered by the enterprise\nagreement or workplace determination.",
      "skos:definition": "(3) The FWC may make a determination under subclause (1) varying\nan enterprise agreement or a workplace determination:\n(a) on its own initiative; or\n(b) on application by any of the following:\n(i) one or more of the employers covered by the enterprise\nagreement or workplace determination;\n\nApplication, saving and transitional provisions relating to amendments of this Act\nSchedule 1\nAmendments made by Part 15 of Schedule 1 to the Fair Work Legislation Amendment\n(Closing Loopholes No. 2) Act 2024  Part 17\nTransitional provisions  Division 2\nClause 120\nFair Work Act 2009\nCompilation date: 02/04/2026\n(ii) an employee covered by the enterprise agreement or\nworkplace determination;\n(iii) an employee organisation covered by the enterprise\nagreement or workplace determination.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:fair-work-act-2009-sch-1-sec-120"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:fair-work-act-2009-sch-1-sec-120-ss-3-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:fair-work-act-2009-sch-1-sec-120-ss-3-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "52db06e39d20bf5962b997560046d813d22d1e4ff33d09c05a0ab23a28b83871",
      "skos:note": "FWC may vary enterprise agreements or workplace determinations."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/fair-work-act-2009#sch-1-sec-120-ss-3",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "120(3) FWC power to deal with uncertainties or difficulties arising",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 108,
      "values:originalText": "(3) The FWC may make a determination under subclause (1) varying\nan enterprise agreement or a workplace determination:\n(a) on its own initiative; or\n(b) on application by any of the following:\n(i) one or more of the employers covered by the enterprise\nagreement or workplace determination;\n\nApplication, saving and transitional provisions relating to amendments of this Act\nSchedule 1\nAmendments made by Part 15 of Schedule 1 to the Fair Work Legislation Amendment\n(Closing Loopholes No. 2) Act 2024  Part 17\nTransitional provisions  Division 2\nClause 120\nFair Work Act 2009\nCompilation date: 02/04/2026\n(ii) an employee covered by the enterprise agreement or\nworkplace determination;\n(iii) an employee organisation covered by the enterprise\nagreement or workplace determination."
    },
