    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:fair-work-act-2009-sch-1-sec-120-ss-6",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "120(6) FWC power to deal with uncertainties or difficulties arising",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/fair-work-act-2009#sch-1-sec-120-ss-6"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "fair-work-act-2009.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "fair-work-act-2009.pdf, p.108",
      "values:originalText": "(6) The regulations may provide as follows:\n(a) that this clause applies, or does not apply, to a specified fair\nwork instrument or a specified class of fair work instrument;\n(b) that this clause applies, or does not apply, to a specified\nuncertainty or difficulty, or a specified class of uncertainty or\ndifficulty.\n\nSchedule 1  Application, saving and transitional provisions relating to amendments of\nthis Act",
      "skos:definition": "(6) The regulations may provide as follows:\n(a) that this clause applies, or does not apply, to a specified fair\nwork instrument or a specified class of fair work instrument;\n(b) that this clause applies, or does not apply, to a specified\nuncertainty or difficulty, or a specified class of uncertainty or\ndifficulty.\n\nSchedule 1  Application, saving and transitional provisions relating to amendments of\nthis Act",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:fair-work-act-2009-sch-1-sec-120"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:fair-work-act-2009-sch-1-sec-120-ss-6-norm"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "93574443903a7a4cac2d2b78133e1eb7e54cd55d2d6ce9c6bab6054de23eb39e",
      "skos:note": "Regulations may provide for specified fair work instruments or uncertainties/difficulties."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/fair-work-act-2009#sch-1-sec-120-ss-6",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "120(6) FWC power to deal with uncertainties or difficulties arising",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 108,
      "values:originalText": "(6) The regulations may provide as follows:\n(a) that this clause applies, or does not apply, to a specified fair\nwork instrument or a specified class of fair work instrument;\n(b) that this clause applies, or does not apply, to a specified\nuncertainty or difficulty, or a specified class of uncertainty or\ndifficulty.\n\nSchedule 1  Application, saving and transitional provisions relating to amendments of\nthis Act"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:fair-work-act-2009-sch-1-sec-120-ss-6-norm",
      "@type": "values:Undertaking",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:fair-work-act-2009-sch-1-sec-120-ss-6"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:fair-work-act-2009-sch-1-sec-122",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "122 Other general provisions about regulations",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/fair-work-act-2009#sch-1-sec-122"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "fair-work-act-2009.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "fair-work-act-2009.pdf, p.110",
      "values:originalText": "(1) This clause applies to regulations made for the purposes of this\nPart.\n(2) Subsection 12(2) (retrospective application of legislative\ninstruments) of the Legislation Act 2003 does not apply to the\nregulations.\n(3) If:\n(a) regulations are expressed to commence from a date (the\nregistration date) before the regulations are registered under\nthe Legislation Act 2003; and\n(b) a person engaged in conduct before the registration date; and\n(c) but for the retrospective effect of the regulations, the conduct\nwould not have contravened a provision of this Act;\n\nApplication, saving and transitional provisions relating to amendments of this Act\nSchedule 1\nAmendments made by Part 15 of Schedule 1 to the Fair Work Legislation Amendment\n(Closing Loopholes No. 2) Act 2024  Part 17\nRegulations about transitional matters  Division 3\nClause 122\nFair Work Act 2009\nCompilation date: 02/04/2026\nthen a court must not convict the person of an offence, or order the\nperson to pay a pecuniary penalty, in relation to the conduct on the\ngrounds that it contravened a provision of this Act.\n\nSchedule 1  Application, saving and transitional provisions relating to amendments of\nthis Act",
      "skos:definition": "(1) This clause applies to regulations made for the purposes of this\nPart.\n(2) Subsection 12(2) (retrospective application of legislative\ninstruments) of the Legislation Act 2003 does not apply to the\nregulations.\n(3) If:\n(a) regulations are expressed to commence from a date (the\nregistration date) before the regulations are registered under\nthe Legislation Act 2003; and\n(b) a person engaged in conduct before the registration date; and\n(c) but for the retrospective effect of the regulations, the conduct\nwould not have contravened a provision of this Act;\n\nApplication, saving and transitional provisions relating to amendments of this Act\nSchedule 1\nAmendments made by Part 15 of Schedule 1 to the Fair Work Legislation Amendment\n(Closing Loopholes No. 2) Act 2024  Part 17\nRegulations about transitional matters  Division 3\nClause 122\nFair Work Act 2009\nCompilation date: 02/04/2026\nthen a court must not convict the person of an offence, or order the\nperson to pay a pecuniary penalty, in relation to the conduct on the\ngrounds that it contravened a provision of this Act.\n\nSchedule 1  Application, saving and transitional provisions relating to amendments of\nthis Act",
      "cml:hasPart": [
