          "@id": "concept:fair-work-act-2009-sch-1-sec-122-ss-3-logic-epistemic-5"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "07ca90661e3f364baa7f68300daf806a304998da0395e6ba1db7afdcbf25e668",
      "skos:note": "Exempts conduct from prosecution if it would not have been a contravention without the retrospective effect of regulations."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/fair-work-act-2009#sch-1-sec-122-ss-3",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "122(3) Other general provisions about regulations",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 110,
      "values:originalText": "(3) If:\n(a) regulations are expressed to commence from a date (the\nregistration date) before the regulations are registered under\nthe Legislation Act 2003; and\n(b) a person engaged in conduct before the registration date; and\n(c) but for the retrospective effect of the regulations, the conduct\nwould not have contravened a provision of this Act;\n\nApplication, saving and transitional provisions relating to amendments of this Act\nSchedule 1\nAmendments made by Part 15 of Schedule 1 to the Fair Work Legislation Amendment\n(Closing Loopholes No. 2) Act 2024  Part 17\nRegulations about transitional matters  Division 3\nClause 122\nFair Work Act 2009\nCompilation date: 02/04/2026\nthen a court must not convict the person of an offence, or order the\nperson to pay a pecuniary penalty, in relation to the conduct on the\ngrounds that it contravened a provision of this Act.\n\nSchedule 1  Application, saving and transitional provisions relating to amendments of\nthis Act"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:fair-work-act-2009-sch-1-sec-122-ss-3-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:fair-work-act-2009-sch-1-sec-122-ss-3"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:State"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:fair-work-act-2009-sch-1-sec-122-ss-3-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Exemption",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Regulations exempt conduct from prosecution if it would not have been a contravention without the retrospective effect of regulations.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(3) If: ... (c) but for the retrospective effect of the regulations, the conduct would not have contravened a provision of this Act;",
      "cml:conclusionText": "then a court must not convict the person of an offence, or order the person to pay a pecuniary penalty, in relation to the conduct on the grounds that it contravened a provision of this Act."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:fair-work-act-2009-sch-1-sec-122-ss-3-logic-alleninterval-2",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:AllenInterval"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Overlaps",
      "cml:logicSummary": "The exemption is related to the temporal interval between registration and commencement dates.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::interval_reasoning",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(3) If: ... (a) regulations are expressed to commence from a date (the registration date) before the regulations are registered under the Legislation Act 2003;",
      "cml:conclusionText": "then a court must not convict the person of an offence, or order the person to pay a pecuniary penalty, in relation to the conduct on the grounds that it contravened a provision of this Act."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:fair-work-act-2009-sch-1-sec-122-ss-3-logic-ltl-3",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:LTL"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Repeats",
      "cml:logicSummary": "The exemption is related to recurring conduct before registration dates.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::temporal_ltl",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(3) If: ... (b) a person engaged in conduct before the registration date;",
      "cml:conclusionText": "then a court must not convict the person of an offence, or order the person to pay a pecuniary penalty, in relation to the conduct on the grounds that it contravened a provision of this Act."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:fair-work-act-2009-sch-1-sec-122-ss-3-logic-deontic-4",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Justification",
      "cml:logicSummary": "The exemption is justified by the retrospective effect of regulations.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(3) If: ... (c) but for the retrospective effect of the regulations, the conduct would not have contravened a provision of this Act;",
      "cml:conclusionText": "then a court must not convict the person of an offence, or order the person to pay a pecuniary penalty, in relation to the conduct on the grounds that it contravened a provision of this Act."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:fair-work-act-2009-sch-1-sec-122-ss-3-logic-epistemic-5",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Epistemic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Belief",
      "cml:logicSummary": "The exemption is believed by courts to be applicable under certain conditions.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::epistemic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(3) If: ... (a) regulations are expressed to commence from a date (the registration date) before the regulations are registered under the Legislation Act 2003;",
      "cml:conclusionText": "then a court must not convict the person of an offence, or order the person to pay a pecuniary penalty, in relation to the conduct on the grounds that it contravened a provision of this Act."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:fair-work-act-2009-sch-1-sec-123",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "123 Definitions",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
