    {
      "@id": "concept:fair-work-act-2009-sch-3-sec-28",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "28 Operation of laws—things done by, or in relation to, FWA",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/fair-work-act-2009#sch-3-sec-28"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "fair-work-act-2009.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "fair-work-act-2009.pdf, p.134",
      "values:originalText": "(1) If, before the commencement of Part 1 of Schedule 9 to the\namending Act, a thing was done by, or in relation to, FWA, then,\nfor the purposes of the operation of any law on or after that\ncommencement, the thing is taken to have been done by, or in\nrelation to, the FWC.\n(2) For the purposes of subclause (1), a thing done before that\ncommencement under a provision amended by Part 1, 2 or 3 of\nSchedule 9 to the amending Act has effect from that\ncommencement as if it were done under that provision as amended.\nHowever, this is not taken to change the time at which the thing\nwas actually done.\n(3) The Minister may, by writing, determine that subclause (1):\n(a) does not apply in relation to a specified thing done by, or in\nrelation to, FWA; or\n(b) applies as if the reference in that subclause to the FWC were\na reference to the President of the FWC; or\n(c) applies as if the reference in that subclause to the FWC were\na reference to another FWC member.\nA determination under this subclause has effect accordingly.\n(4) A determination made under subclause (3) is not a legislative\ninstrument.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) If, before the commencement of Part 1 of Schedule 9 to the\namending Act, a thing was done by, or in relation to, FWA, then,\nfor the purposes of the operation of any law on or after that\ncommencement, the thing is taken to have been done by, or in\nrelation to, the FWC.\n(2) For the purposes of subclause (1), a thing done before that\ncommencement under a provision amended by Part 1, 2 or 3 of\nSchedule 9 to the amending Act has effect from that\ncommencement as if it were done under that provision as amended.\nHowever, this is not taken to change the time at which the thing\nwas actually done.\n(3) The Minister may, by writing, determine that subclause (1):\n(a) does not apply in relation to a specified thing done by, or in\nrelation to, FWA; or\n(b) applies as if the reference in that subclause to the FWC were\na reference to the President of the FWC; or\n(c) applies as if the reference in that subclause to the FWC were\na reference to another FWC member.\nA determination under this subclause has effect accordingly.\n(4) A determination made under subclause (3) is not a legislative\ninstrument.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:fair-work-act-2009-sch-3-sec-28-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:fair-work-act-2009-sch-3-sec-28-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:fair-work-act-2009-sch-3-sec-28-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:fair-work-act-2009-sch-3-sec-28-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "ff97ad434a2dd052bb23e725fa95efa513416fd7b7191918118c0047b859ef4a"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/fair-work-act-2009#sch-3-sec-28",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "28 Operation of laws—things done by, or in relation to, FWA",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 134,
      "values:originalText": "(1) If, before the commencement of Part 1 of Schedule 9 to the\namending Act, a thing was done by, or in relation to, FWA, then,\nfor the purposes of the operation of any law on or after that\ncommencement, the thing is taken to have been done by, or in\nrelation to, the FWC.\n(2) For the purposes of subclause (1), a thing done before that\ncommencement under a provision amended by Part 1, 2 or 3 of\nSchedule 9 to the amending Act has effect from that\ncommencement as if it were done under that provision as amended.\nHowever, this is not taken to change the time at which the thing\nwas actually done.\n(3) The Minister may, by writing, determine that subclause (1):\n(a) does not apply in relation to a specified thing done by, or in\nrelation to, FWA; or\n(b) applies as if the reference in that subclause to the FWC were\na reference to the President of the FWC; or\n(c) applies as if the reference in that subclause to the FWC were\na reference to another FWC member.\nA determination under this subclause has effect accordingly.\n(4) A determination made under subclause (3) is not a legislative\ninstrument."
    },
